0,Gowlan (The Word for the World International) | South Asia Bibles,https://southasiabibles.com/resource/language/gowlan,"Gowlan is classified as a spurious language by wikipedia. According to Ethnologue there are 20,200 speakers as of 2000. Gowlan is an Indo-European (Indo-Germanische, Indo-Hittite) language.",Gowlan,Indo-European
1,Gowlan Language (GOJ) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/goj/,"Gowlan is a stable indigenous language of India. It belongs to the Indo-European language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.",Gowlan,Indo-European
2,Gowlan — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/gowlan,"[2] It belongs to the Indo-European language family and is classified by some sources as a stable indigenous variety used at home by the ethnic community. [3] Reported dialects include Karnataka Gowlan and Maharashtra Gowlan, but their distinctiveness is unclear.",Gowlan,Indo-European
